   "notes": "Only original lattice parameters, printed errors and pressure columns are reported observations. Volume a^3 and its first-order error 3a^2*error(a), path assignment, and NaCl phase are curator derivations. Printed 0.0000 errors remain literal zeros (not exact measurements); missing errors remain blank. No pressure uncertainties are invented. The fp39 mw39c block is decompression (paragraph 8/Figure 2 and reversed pressure sequence); no separate decompression EOS is published. For mw58 at >=44 GPa the scalar a_mw58 does not specify a full rhombohedral cell, so volume and its error are deliberately blank. The 42.75 GPa B1 row is retained and included under the explicit assumption that the caption's approximately 42 GPa HS endpoint refers to this row. Linked full tables contain observations outside the fitted branch; use record validation_selection explicitly."
